{"format":1,"key":"zone:wetlands","path":"/lore/zone/wetlands","name":"Wetlands","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"wetlands","name":"Wetlands","path":"/lore/zone/wetlands"},"levels":"Levels 20-30","description":"The Wetlands is a vast, mist-shrouded swamp nestled between the mountains of Khaz Modan and the shores of Baradin Bay. Historically battered by dwarven…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:wetlands","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["The Wetlands is a vast, mist-shrouded swamp nestled between the mountains of Khaz Modan and the shores of Baradin Bay. Historically battered by dwarven wars and orcish invasions, it serves as a rugged buffer zone between Ironforge and the northern lands of Lordaeron. The fortified port of Menethil Harbor stands as the Alliance's primary lifeline in a sodden wilderness overrun by Dragonmaw orcs, murlocs, and gnolls.","Spreading out beneath the towering precipice of the Stonewrought Dam, the Wetlands is a cold, waterlogged expanse cloaked in perpetual fog and uniform gray skies. While once home to thriving dwarven settlements, the marshlands are now scattered with sunken stone ruins, sodden bogs, and treacherous mires. Adventurers entering the region must navigate narrow passes, either coming north through the barricaded defile of Dun Algaz from Loch Modan or crossing the towering arches of the Thandol Span from the Arathi Highlands.","The eastern reaches of the swamp are dominated by the brooding presence of Grim Batol, the former Wildhammer stronghold. After its defilement during the War of the Three Hammers, it became the fortified redoubt of the Dragonmaw clan during the Second War. When the red dragonflight broke free from orcish captivity, their fiery vengeance shattered the orcish forces and laid waste to the surrounding slopes. Today, red wyrmkin guard the Dragonmaw Gates against all trespassers, while feral remnants of the Dragonmaw clan dwell in scattered hill camps, continuing to harass travellers across the swamp.","Perched on the rim of Baradin Bay, Menethil Harbor is the beating heart of Alliance trade and logistics in Khaz Modan. Named in honor of King Terenas Menethil II, this stalwart port connects the Eastern Kingdoms to distant Kalimdor through regular transport ships sailing to Theramore Isle and, by way of Southshore, to Auberdine. Despite its strategic military importance and solid dwarven architecture, the harbor is perpetually under threat from coastal murlocs, swamp creatures, and coastal raiders who prey on vessels navigating the rocky channels.","The Wetlands is an active war zone on multiple fronts. In the far north, Dark Iron dwarves under the warlock Balgaras the Foul have sabotage-bombed the Thandol Span and overrun the town of Dun Modr, cutting off overland supply trains. Meanwhile, Mosshide gnolls run rampant through the central fens, threatening even ancient protectors like Rethiel the Greenwarden. Between rogue orc warbands, Dark Iron infiltrators, and cursed shipwrecks along the coast, holding the swamp requires constant vigilance."],"hash":"22678f","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"03d7dc1e4e","sec":148},"female-narrator":{"sha":"780f4a9af7","sec":162}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Wetlands (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wetlands_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Wetlands","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wetlands"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/menethil-harbor","n":"Menethil Harbor","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/grim-batol","n":"Grim Batol","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dun-modr","n":"Dun Modr","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/thandol-span","n":"Thandol Span","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dun-algaz","n":"Dun Algaz","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/topic/dragonmaw-clan","n":"Dragonmaw clan","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/npc/rethiel-the-greenwarden","n":"Rethiel the Greenwarden","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/quest/455-the-algaz-gauntlet","n":"The Algaz Gauntlet","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/